CFG172D_A1 -- the theta equation of 11C-d, re-derived (not assumed): H-i, H-ii, T-d1, the d2 pincer formula, O3 (a,b,c), C7.

WHAT THIS SCRIPT DOES (frozen criteria section 6, A1; nothing here is tuned):
  S1 [sympy, spherical, exact] The khronon's tau-variation of V0's covariant brace with f = F(theta): tau = t + eps*pi(t,r) on the
     metric -N^2 dt^2 + a(t)^2 A(r)^2 (dr^2 + r^2 dOmega^2), all leafwise auxiliaries generic functions of (t,r).  L1 = dL/deps at
     eps = 0 is split into the theta channel (dL/dTheta * delta theta: gives the conjugate Pi and the operator
     div[h grad Pi / sqrt(-X)]) and the REST (every other tau-dependence: leafwise Laplacians, projected gradients, the
     4-acceleration, eps_d = u u T).  H-i (criteria 1.3) says REST = 0.  It is tested (i) in the static, non-expanding limit and
     (ii) with adot != 0 (quasi-static fields).  H-ii says alpha_c enters only through time derivatives: tested by extracting the
     alpha_c-dependence of REST.
  S2 [sympy] T-d1 (Pi constant on a leaf when REST = 0 => the same theta on both plateaus) and the d2 reduction: integrate out
     delta-theta, the interaction energy, c_gate^2, and the pincer formula -c_s^2/c^2 = 3 c2 Delta^2 eps_L/eps_b.
  S3 [numeric] C7: any C^2 flat-flat gate has f'' of both signs; W'' extrema.
  O3a [sympy] the NR Lagrangian's Euler-Lagrange equations with f = f(r) generic (Phi = u + f P, lam = -f Psi, kernel reads w).
  O3b [numeric] homogeneous background off-plateau for u_theta, w in {0.25, 1}, z in [-0.5..20] (criteria O3b).
  O3c [sympy] the local Hessian of the constraint system with the theta row (Schur complement on theta).
MUTATE=M6 (drop the leaf-mean offset): O3b must FAIL for w = 1.     MUTATE=M7 (c2 -> -c2, a ghost theta sector): the theta-theta
Hessian entry changes sign; the stability claim must FAIL.   exit 1 when the control bites.

  repo: <repo>/.   MUTATE=M6

==============================================================================================================
S1  THE TAU-VARIATION OF V0 WITH f = F(theta), DERIVED SYMBOLICALLY (H-i, H-ii)
==============================================================================================================
  Lagrangian, theta channel and REST built (1 s); theta_0 = 3*Derivative(a(t), t)/(N(r)*a(t)) (the background expansion 3 adot/(N a)), theta_1 = -div of the tilt: (-r*A(r)*N(r)*Derivative(pi(t, r), (r, 2)) - 2*r*A(r)*Derivative(N(r), r)*Derivative(pi(t, r), r) - r*N(r)*Derivative(A(r), r)*Derivative(pi(t, r), r) - 2*A(r)*N(r)*Derivative(pi(t, r), r))/(r*A(r)**3*a(t)**2)
  E-L operators built (6 s)
  E-L[REST] in the static, non-expanding limit (all time derivatives and adot set to 0): 0
  [PASS] H-i (static limit) the MOND-sector, C-H chassis, alpha_c, projected-gradient and eps_d terms give NO O(pi) source when the background is static and non-expanding
         E-L[REST] = 0
  E-L[REST] with adot != 0 (fields static in comoving r): a polynomial in adot of degree 2; lam^0 coefficient = 0
  [FAIL] (reported) H-i (expanding background, quasi-static fields): E-L[REST] = 0
         FALSE as written: E-L[REST] is a polynomial of degree 2 in adot with zero adot^0 part, i.e. an O(H) MOND-sector source of theta exists; H-i holds only in the static limit (its size is estimated in A2)
  alpha_c dependence: d(E-L[REST])/d alpha_c has lam^0 coefficient 0 (i.e. zero without adot) and degree 1 in adot
  [PASS] H-ii alpha_c enters the theta-equation's remainder only multiplied by adot (a time derivative)
         lam^0 coefficient of dE/d(alpha_c) = 0; nonzero adot-part: True
  theta channel: E-L[Pihat*sqrt(-g)*delta theta] = r*(-r*A(r)*N(r)*Derivative(Pihat(t, r), (r, 2)) - 2*r*A(r)*Derivative(N(r), r)*Derivative(Pihat(t, r), r) - r*N(r)*Derivative(A(r), r)*Derivative(Pihat(t, r), r) - 2*A(r)*N(r)*Derivative(Pihat(t, r), r))*N(r)*a(t)
  compared with -d/dr(a N^2 A r^2 dPihat/dr): difference = 0
  [PASS] the theta channel gives div[h grad Pi / sqrt(-X)] (the khronon's flow equation), Pi = dL/dtheta per unit sqrt(-g)
         difference 0
  REST with V = Lm = Ld = 0 (no dark component, no filter), quasi-static: 295 operations; saved for A2's size estimate

==============================================================================================================
S2  T-d1 AND THE d2 PINCER (symbolic)
==============================================================================================================
  Pi(theta) = Bcal*Derivative(f(theta), theta) - 16*pi*G*rho*zeta*Subs(Derivative(h(_xi_1), _xi_1), _xi_1, (theta - thetabar)/thetaL)/(c**2*thetaL) - c2*(2*theta - 2*thetabar)
  plateau (f' = 0, zeta = 0): Pi = Pi0 => theta = [-Pi0/(2*c2) + thetabar]: independent of position => the same value on every plateau
  [PASS] T-d1: on any plateau of f (f' = 0), Pi = Pi0 forces theta = thetabar - Pi0/(2 c2), the same number on the bound and the web plateaus (so d1 cannot be a region gate)
         theta = -Pi0/(2*c2) + thetabar
  d2(lin): delta theta* = -8*pi*G*rho*zeta/(c**2*c2*thetaL); energy density E_int = -4*pi*G*rho**2*zeta**2/(c2*thetaL**2)
  E_int (thetaL^2 = 3 Lambda) = -4*pi*G*rho**2*zeta**2/(3*Lambda*c2);  c_s^2 = rho d2E/drho2 = -8*pi*G*rho*zeta**2/(3*Lambda*c2)
  c_s^2/c^2 with rho -> eps_b/c^2: -epsb*zeta**2/(3*c2*epsL)
  [PASS] d2 pincer (frozen criteria 3.2): c_s^2/c^2 = -zeta^2 eps_b/(3 c2 eps_Lambda)
         derived -epsb*zeta**2/(3*c2*epsL); frozen -epsb*zeta**2/(3*c2*epsL)
  eliminating zeta through the depletion Delta = |delta theta|/thetaL = zeta eps_b/(3 c2 eps_L): -c_s^2/c^2 = 3*Delta**2*c2*epsL/epsb
  [PASS] d2 pincer formula: -c_s^2/c^2 = 3 c2 Delta^2 eps_L/eps_b, independent of zeta
         3*Delta**2*c2*epsL/epsb
  L_thth = Bcal*Derivative(f(theta), (theta, 2)) - 16*pi*G*rho*zeta*Subs(Derivative(h(_xi_1), (_xi_1, 2)), _xi_1, theta/thetaL - thetabar/thetaL)/(c**2*thetaL**2) - 2*c2 (the gate adds B f''; a fold where L_thth -> 0 divides c_gate^2 by |L_thth|)

